    "done_when": "WallOutline2D and VesselShell live in imas_ink/_types.py, extract_vessel_shells in imas_ink/extract.py and _offset_polygon in imas_ink/geometry.py; imas_ink/three_d/walls.py imports them from there and its private _safe_float is deleted; the lazy name map in imas_ink/__init__.py points VesselShell, WallOutline2D and extract_vessel_shells at their new modules; extract_vessel_shells takes the description_2d entry to read (index 0 when none is given), reads thickness through imas_ink._sentinel.safe_float, and returns one VesselShell per filled annular outline_inner and outline_outer (inner then outer) ahead of the unchanged centreline and outline paths; extract_geometry passes the entry _select_description_2d chose and fills a new MachineGeometry field of VesselShell objects; MachineGeometry.viewport includes the vessel shells' bounds; the WallOutline component carries the shells, _render_wall_alt gains the wall_units loop _render_wall_mpl has, and both renderers draw the shells as unfilled lines with wall_color and wall_linewidth; geometry_figure_mpl passes the shells to the WallOutline it builds; tests/unit/test_vessel_units.py builds a wall IDS with one limiter unit and one vessel unit whose annular outline_inner and outline_outer are filled and asserts: extract_vessel_shells returns two closed shells; a geometry whose richest description_2d entry is not index 0 takes its vessel from that entry; geometry_figure_mpl adds both shells' lines to the axes; a vessel skin outside the coil and limiter extent lies inside the axes limits; _render_wall_alt emits a mark for every limiter unit and both shells; importing imas_ink.extract and imas_ink.figures leaves imas_ink.three_d out of sys.modules; 'uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/unit tests/three_d' adds no failure against the base revision, and 'uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ink tests' exits 0",
